 health conditions are dangerous or weak, which only serves to further marginalize and isolate those who are struggling. This unjust discrimination can lead to feelings of shame, embarrassment, and guilt, making it incredibly difficult for individuals to open up about their struggles and seek the help they need. Raising awareness about mental health is crucial in combating stigma. Education and open conversations can dispel myths and provide accurate information about mental health conditions. By promoting understanding, empathy, and acceptance, we can create a more inclusive and supportive society for individuals living with mental illness. Additionally, it is essential to encourage people to seek mental health support without fear of judgment. Creating safe spaces and destigmatizing mental health treatment can empower individuals to reach out for help and access the resources they need to live healthier, happier lives. In conclusion, mental health awareness and stigma go hand in hand. By increasing understanding and challenging societal misconceptions, we can create a world where mental health is treated with the same importance as physical health. It is only through this collective effort that we can work towards eradicating mental health stigma and providing compassionate care for all. Awareness is the first step towards change.", "encoded_message": "Psychological Wellness Understanding along with Disgrace. Mental hygiene represents one essential dimension regarding whole good health, still the condition is commonly omitted and discredited within culture. That absence of awareness and comprehension encompassing psychological health illnesses leads to the continuation of stigma and prejudice. Such stigma may possess destructive results regarding people's existences, obstructing these individuals free from in quest of assistance and reinforcement whenever those demand this support to the greatest extent. An of the primary justifications concerning mental health stain is the misunderstandings and typecasts connected with mental disease. Individuals might assume that individuals with mental health conditions are viewed perilous or alternatively feeble, this merely functions toward increased sideline and separate such that remain grappling. The aforementioned unwarranted discrimination can lead to feelings of shame, embarrassment, and guilt, making it incredibly difficult for individuals to open up about their struggles and seek the help they need. Raising awareness about mental health is crucial in combating stigma. Education and open conversations can dispel myths and provide accurate information about mental health conditions. By promoting understanding, empathy, and acceptance, we can create a more inclusive and supportive society for individuals living with mental illness. Additionally, it is essential to encourage people to seek mental health support without fear of judgment. Creating safe spaces and destigmatizing mental health treatment can empower individuals to reach out for help and access the resources they need to live healthier, happier lives. In conclusion, mental health awareness and stigma go hand in hand. By increasing understanding and challenging societal misconceptions, we can create a world where mental health is treated with the same importance as physical health. It is only through this collective effort that we can work towards eradicating mental health stigma and providing compassionate care for all. Awareness is the first step towards change.", "encoding_time_report": {"container_generation": 25.71, "secret_key_generation": 57.53}, "decoding_time": 0.0006878376007080078, "decoded_message": "00110010011111101110110101011100001110000000010000001000101011001010110010010010010001110010100000000011111000001011001001010111", "error_message": ""}